WEBVTT

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.360
The monster who ruled postwar 
Japan from the shadows,

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.550
Washizu Iwao.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.390
His limitless money.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.610
In his spacious downtown mansion, 
a veritable symbol of his wealth,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.840
a deathmatch was about to begin.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.970
<b>Episode 16</b>

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.970
<b>The Mahjong Game of Destruction</b>

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:30.600
That fateful night,

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:36.140
August 31, 1965, at 10:30 PM.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:40.910
The one to challenge the monster 
is the genius called Akagi Shigeru.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.190
That's what I want to see.

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:47.620
That fear, that horror.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.320
So badly that I've killed 
so many men already!

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.060
<i>He's crazy.</i>

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.680
<i>It's in a different way from 
Akagi, but he's also crazy.</i>

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.290
<i>His heart is no longer human.</i>

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.280
<i>He's a monster.</i>

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:07.330
Washizu will bet 20 million on this game.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:13.830
20 million in 1965 would be 
more than 200 million today.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.490
Akagi will wager 2,000 CCs of blood,

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.270
the loss of which is enough to kill him.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.300
2,000 CCs of blood translates 
to 200,000 points.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.170
Here is the apparatus that makes 
our game tonight possible,

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.520
the tool that will draw 
out Akagi-kun's blood.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.940
You can just think of it 
as a gigantic syringe.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.120
The blood is withdrawn by reducing 
pressure from the inside of the tubes.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:02.000
Each of these holds exactly 250 CCs.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:07.460
After the sixth tube, which would be 
1,500 CCs, death will start to creep in.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:13.130
And you'll probably expire before 
we can fill the eighth tube.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:21.640
These tubes represent the years of life 
you will be investing in this game.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.060
Simply put, if we say you'll die

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.150
somewhere between 
the sixth and eighth tubes,

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:29.150
each tube is a decade of your life.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.150
That is to say, you will be living 
an entire life's worth of time

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.650
in the few hours that are to come.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.700
You'll be stepping onto a path of 
carnage from which there is no return.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.400
Should you lose eight tubes 
along the way, you die,

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.800
and no sympathy will be 
spared for your state.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.650
You may beg, you may scream, 
but you will still die.

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:52.400
What do you say?

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.910
Sounds good to me.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.190
The problem lies ahead.

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:00.140
Ahead?

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.050
There is one thing I would like changed.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.620
That rate isn't enough.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.350
It can't destroy you.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.410
What?

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.950
The only way to destroy you is 
to change the order of magnitude.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.330
I want the wager to be increased tenfold.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.450
Ridiculous!

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:26.430
Stop talking nonsense!

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:29.540
You want me to wager 200 million 
on the life of some worthless punk?

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:36.850
200 million in 1965 would 
be over 2 billion today.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.520
No, that's out of the question.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.970
I know that even 20 million is way beyond

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.090
the worth of a street punk like myself.

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:51.860
My problem is that you are 
diluting my life's value

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.130
by equating it to 200,000 points.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:58.910
20 million yen shouldn't 
be worth 200,000 points.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:02.030
Make it worth 20,000 points instead.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:08.340
Should I win 500,000 points, I could 
take away 500 million from you.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.680
That would be five billion today.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:13.180
Then you're within reach.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.150
Your destruction will be within reach.

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:19.580
Are you stupid?

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.960
That is impossible!

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.300
How do you expect to survive six 
East-South matches with only 20,000 points?

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.860
The ranking bonus alone 
is 10,000 and 30,000!

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:29.270
If I'm ahead of you in a single match,

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:32.330
that alone will give me a rank bonus 
of 20,000, and you'll be dead.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:36.990
You'll have to place higher than 
me in all six East-South matches!

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:39.080
And then there's that 
bonus I talked about.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.480
I can withdraw blood from you any time

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.040
I get a tsumo or a direct hit off of you!

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.040
If you deal into two of my mangan hands,

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.540
right then, that's 16,000 
points. 1,600 CCs!

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.390
You'd be facing death in one fell swoop.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:54.380
There's no way you could survive.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.360
It wouldn't be really impossible.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.090
What?

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:09.390
First off, if you don't set 20 million 
to correspond to 20,000 points,

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.870
there is no way that I can kill you.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.240
What is wrong with him?

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.390
Who does he think he's talking to?

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:19.980
Ougi!

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:25.920
Explain to this piece of 
trash exactly who I am,

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.920
and that this is no mere game!

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:35.430
Washizu-sama, I apologize for 
Akagi's rude way of speaking.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:40.380
However, the one who is 
misunderstanding the nature

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:42.500
of tonight's game is you.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:44.770
Misunderstanding?

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.400
Correct.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:52.920
We came here tonight for a genuine battle.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.860
This man here is different 
from the sacrificial lambs

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:59.160
we have brought you in the past.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:02.950
Akagi can overcome any disadvantage.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:06.960
That is to say, he could 
potentially survive six

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.370
East-South matches on 
only 20,000 points.

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:13.180
That's what we had in mind 
when we prepared this...

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:14.200
...assassin.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:22.410
He's the one who will kill you.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:25.410
What?

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:28.140
Are you serious?

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:31.110
An assassin to kill me?

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:34.380
A genuine battle?

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:38.410
Who do you think you're talking to, Ougi?

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:43.420
You dare show such insolence to 
the true ruler of this country?

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:47.360
To me, Washizu Iwao?!

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:52.700
I will crush you, Ougi.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:56.870
Forgive me, but I believe 
that is no longer the case.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:00.760
Some time ago, you may 
have said the same thing

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.340
and it would have been 
undoubtedly true.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.520
But it is far from true now.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.180
You've used up much of 
your fortune to silence

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:11.820
and bribe various politicians and members

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.890
of the police force in this investigation.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:20.270
All you have left now is this mansion 
and some amount of securities and bonds.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:26.320
According to our sources, 
these assets value around 500 million.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:32.910
Considering what you were 
once worth, it's peanuts.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:39.840
You only have enough left to 
run away to another country.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:41.950
You're just a nouveau riche 
fleeing the capital.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.950
You don't scare anyone anymore.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.400
Ougi!

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.460
You bastard.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:53.260
We've taken off our obedient 
sheep masks for tonight

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.370
and we're here to take 
your entire fortune.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.970
All of the 500 million that you have left.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:04.570
We ask that you bring that money here.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:09.750
We want you to wager the very last 
of your fortune on this game.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:15.490
A human life should be 
worth that much at least.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.150
If Akagi's destruction is 
on the line for this game,

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:22.660
you should have to do no less.

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:26.160
We ask that you please accept 
this tenfold increase.

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:30.530
That you make the 20,000 
points worth 20 million yen.

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:34.320
The game in which Akagi will 
either take your 500 million

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.030
with 500,000 points,

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:42.070
or you'll take his life with 20,000 points.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.850
It will be a game in which you 
mutually bet your own demise.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.500
That's insane!

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.450
You're asking me to 
bet my entire fortune?

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:52.650
What about you?

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.850
Are you all talk?

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.560
I'm betting my entire fortune;

00:09:56.560 --> 00:10:01.210
this kid is betting enough blood to die, 
but you've got nothing to lose.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:02.530
It's ridiculous.

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:05.820
I can't allow you to oversee this game

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:09.370
if you're nothing but empty words.

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:11.340
I simply can't allow it!

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:25.640
Your arm.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.190
Bet your arm, Ougi!

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:32.690
<i>Ougi...</i>

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:47.870
The moment Akagi dies, 
you lose one of your arms.

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:49.740
That's fine.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:58.180
You should know that in Washizu 
Mahjong, death is defeat.

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:00.250
When that piece of trash dies,

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:03.690
any amount he has amassed 
to that point is void.

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:05.840
If he dies, I will reclaim that money.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.670
You won't receive a single yen.

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:11.230
What I'm saying is, if the kid dies, 
you won't get any money.

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.870
All you'll get is one less arm.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.960
Are you all right with that?

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:19.430
That's fine.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:32.660
Get it ready.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:33.620
Sir?

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:34.870
The money.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.640
The 500 million.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.350
Washizu-sama.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:40.350
Please remain calm.

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.570
What?!

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.580
Should you lose that money...

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:45.970
I won't!

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:49.030
He only has 20,000 points 
for six East-South matches.

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:52.600
I need outrank him in only 
one, and it's all over.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.410
Paying the ranking bonus 
alone will destroy him.

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:56.600
Washizu-sama...

00:11:56.600 --> 00:11:58.730
There is no way I can lose!

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.430
There's not even the slightest 
chance of me losing!

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:01.820
Am I wrong?

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.330
It is as you say.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:09.250
It's unthinkable that you would lose 
this wager under these conditions.

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:15.960
It is unthinkable... But even 
knowing that, you need insurance.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:16.930
Insurance?

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:17.620
Yes.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:23.130
It was upon that bedrock 
that your life was built.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:27.370
Are you saying I should ignore all 
the insults they have hurled at me?

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.030
No, but for safety's sake,

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:36.760
what if you were to reduce the game 
from six East-South matches to two?

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:38.110
If you do that, no matter 
how much you lose...

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:39.220
That's ridiculous!

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:41.110
Then they'll get away with 
whatever they have at that point!

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:46.240
To prevent that, we could have a 
rule where you alone can choose

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:49.120
to continue or stop the game 
every two East-South matches.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.120
How does that sound?

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:53.360
If at the end of two East-South matches,

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:57.960
you need only a tiny push to 
kill him, you can keep going.

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.830
But if the game is not in your favor

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:02.320
and it is looking dangerous, 
you can stop there.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.600
There is nothing cowardly about this.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:10.340
A battle of this magnitude requires 
this bare minimum of insurance.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:14.130
Besides, it was they who 
made the ridiculous suggestion

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:15.850
to raise the wager tenfold.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:20.080
It is only natural for you 
to get this privilege.

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:22.590
I beg you to consider this.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:30.590
In the end, Washizu took this advice 
and asked Ougi to accept these terms.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:34.320
Accepting Washizu's clause 
to escape at any time

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:37.220
is nothing but a demerit for Ougi's side.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.300
What should we do?

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:47.910
No point asking.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:49.050
It's probably all the same.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.280
The same?

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:52.890
It can stop at the second East-South match,

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:54.880
or we can continue.

00:13:54.880 --> 00:13:57.580
Having the right decide that

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:00.240
means nothing once the game starts.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:05.620
The last of his fortune is going to 
start shifting hands in the millions.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:07.790
Once he gets started, 
he won't be able to stop.

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:10.900
He'll go as far as he can.

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:15.630
It's a pointless rule.

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:17.660
If anything it's the other way around.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:18.640
The other way around?

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:21.050
He tied his own noose.

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:24.030
Washizu is digging his own 
grave with this special rule.

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:26.650
It's a foolish condition that kills 
his own chance of winning.

00:14:44.930 --> 00:14:47.190
Akagi is betting his life blood,

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:50.540
and Washizu is betting his 
own brand of life blood,

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:51.340
his last 500 million,

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:58.010
worth over five billion today.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.680
Both parties have wagered 
their own destruction

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:04.500
in this deathmatch of insanity.

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:09.690
Then let's begin.

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:16.830
That's all you get.

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:18.990
Those points are your everything.

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:22.640
The 20,000 points that correspond 
to your 2,000 CCs of blood.

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:25.440
And when you lose them, you die.

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:34.180
Why don't you roll the 
dice to decide the dealer.

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:39.230
No walls are built in Washizu Mahjong.

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:42.620
The dice are used only to 
determine who is dealer.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.050
Once the dealer is decided,

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:47.140
each player will take turns 
drawing two tiles from a hole,

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:50.660
wearing leather gloves to prevent 
feeling which tile is grabbed.

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:52.080
These will be their starting hands.

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.890
Once this is done, the dealer 
will draw the dora indicator

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:58.000
and place it in its slot.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:02.670
This is how Washizu Mahjong starts.

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:08.720
<i>What is the most effective 
playing style in a game</i>

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:10.880
<i>where everyone can see your tiles?</i>

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.130
<i>I can't even begin to imagine it.</i>

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:16.620
<i>But we've got to stay on the defensive.</i>

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.780
<i>We've got to keep our defense 
up all the way through.</i>

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:23.410
What Ougi is hoping for is 
an impenetrable defense.

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:25.630
A seal that will not allow a 
single drop of water to leak.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:30.130
<i>Without that, those 20,000 points 
will be gone in the blink of an eye.</i>

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:36.630
<i>It's not just direct hits that make him 
lose blood, but tsumo wins, as well.</i>

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.190
<i>His life blood...</i>

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:43.110
<i>I can't wait.</i>

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:47.720
<i>I really am excited to see how he plays.</i>

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.830
<i>He sure talked big.</i>

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:54.270
<i>He better play big, too.</i>

00:16:54.270 --> 00:17:00.480
<i>Then again, an ordinary 
player would barely survive</i>

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:04.560
<i>with 200,000 points, let alone 20,000.</i>

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:07.510
<i>Having only that many points is insane.</i>

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:10.920
<i>It's so crazy that it's 
tantamount to suicide.</i>

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:19.680
<i>To have even a 1% chance to survive, 
you'd have to be a genius.</i>

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.320
<i>And not just any ordinary genius.</i>

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.050
<i>He'll need intuition 
beyond human understanding.</i>

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:27.790
<i>Perception that overwhelms all others.</i>

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:32.860
<i>A mastery that might as well 
be in the divine realm.</i>

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:35.300
<i>He will also need to be insane.</i>

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:38.010
<i>He'll need to be devoid of all reason.</i>

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:40.400
<i>He'll need to be broken 
as a human being.</i>

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:45.510
<i>No matter what happens, 
he must show absolutely no fear.</i>

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:50.010
<i>So do you possess this madness, Akagi?</i>

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:53.800
On the seventh turn, 
Washizu enters tenpai.

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:57.150
<i>An auspicious start.</i>

00:17:57.150 --> 00:18:00.080
<i>I'll get to test him early in the game.</i>

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:03.530
Riichi.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:04.860
<i>There it is.</i>

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:06.710
<i>Washizu's preemptive riichi.</i>

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:09.030
<i>The riichi he absolutely cannot deal into!</i>

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:16.540
When playing with transparent tiles, 
a riichi becomes much less terrifying.

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:20.780
<i>Being able to see this much 
reduces the possible waits.</i>

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.500
<i>A 1 or 4 of characters; 
a 1, 4, or 7 of bamboo;</i>

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.410
<i>or a 3 or 6 of bamboo.</i>

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:27.410
And on the same seventh turn...

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:32.180
Akagi comes right back.

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:35.020
If he discards the 4 of characters, 
he'll be in tenpai with a 4/7 of circles wait.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:38.010
<i>The 4 of characters 
is one of the few tiles</i>

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:40.120
<i>that Washizu may be waiting on.</i>

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.440
<i>If you think about it,</i>

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:43.570
<i>those discarded 2 and 3 of characters</i>

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:46.470
<i>might be a trap to get 
Akagi to discard the 4.</i>

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:50.270
<i>The only thing to do here is to 
quietly move the game along...</i>

00:18:56.620 --> 00:18:58.640
<i>Yes. That's the ticket.</i>

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:06.820
Akagi plays it safe.

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:12.890
He discards the 5 and 6 of circles, keeping 
the 4 of characters, and is back in tenpai.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:14.030
<i>Here it is.</i>

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:17.030
Yasuoka deals into his hand...

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:18.150
Ron.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.530
...and he avoids Washizu's preemptive riichi.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:24.270
Pinfu, one dora. 2,000.

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:27.320
<i>Yes. That's good.</i>

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:28.270
<i>This is the best way.</i>

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:31.950
<i>Tighten your defenses and 
slip through the cracks to win.</i>

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:33.720
<i>This is the right way.</i>

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.320
How boring.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.900
You won't survive that way.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:43.760
You'll die if you play like that.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.600
Think about it.

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.600
If you had dealt that 4 of characters

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.480
instead of the 6 of circles, 
and gone into tenpai,

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:55.290
I would've played into 
your hand immediately.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:59.420
With a mentanpin, ippatsu, and 
one dora, you'd have had a mangan.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:02.030
A haneman, if you got any reverse dora.

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:04.270
And you let it slip away.

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:08.790
You let that go in order to get a pathetic 
2,000 points from your partner.

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:10.910
The worst kind of game.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:13.280
You're wrong.

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.040
That worked fine for here.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.020
Nothing would have been better.

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:19.650
It's easy for Washizu to talk after the fact.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.180
Don't let him get to you, Akagi.

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:27.060
He's just trying to taunt you 
so you'll go on the offensive.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:31.470
Maybe he's trying to taunt me,

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:35.100
but what he's saying 
is fundamentally true.

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:42.110
It's not that simple, though.

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:47.900
You'll realize it soon enough.

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:56.490
And thus, Washizu Mahjong has begun.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:01.070
Who will be destroyed: 
Akagi or Washizu?

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:04.240
It's a path of carnage with no 
possibility of turning back.

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:08.170
The one-way battle has begun.

00:22:16.370 --> 00:22:18.800
Next time, "The Proof of Genius."

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>The Proof of Genius</b>
